"""The incident rows behind benefit_incidents.md. benefit_incidents.py validates and computes from them.

Each row: id, cls, rec, quote, cost, then keyword fields.
cls   A, B, C, D, E. cause (A only): actual, symptom.
rec   a path under the repo, or git:<sha> for a commit message. quote must occur there verbatim,
      whitespace runs collapsed; benefit_incidents.py refuses a row whose quote does not.
file, phrase   a single-line fragment of the false or useful text, for `git log -S` and the block lookup.
origin   birth (false when written), drift (a later change made it false), unknown.
same     True when the text was written in the step that found it.
rule     N: the rule's form allows this text, so a rule on new comments changes nothing; only review
         could. F: the form is one the rule bars (per-step reading, line number, closed-step promise,
         a number nothing reads, narration), so it bites only if in force when the text was written.
         U: the record does not settle it.
script   S: a script could flag it without reading behaviour (dead file:line, gone path, closed id,
         number against its command or its test). R: needs a reader of behaviour. U: unsettled.
"""

